course: dictionary
lesson: 14639
title: Precaution
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A precaution is something you do before something bad can happen, to stop it or make it less likely. The word has «pre» in it, which means before. Look for clues like «in case», «to stop», or «to protect», because they often show that someone is preparing for a problem.
explain: «Lily wore her helmet before she cycled down the hill.» The helmet is a precaution. Lily did not wait for a fall. She protected her head in advance, so it would be safer if she fell.
explain: «Dad took an umbrella with him, as a precaution, in case it rained.» Dad did not know for sure that it would rain. He prepared just in case. Ask yourself: did the person act before the problem, or after? If it was before, it is probably a precaution.
fact: A precaution is something you do in advance to stop something bad or dangerous from happening.
fact: «Precautions» is the plural, meaning more than one precaution.
fact: Common phrases are take precautions, as a precaution, safety precautions and fire precautions.
fact: Wearing goggles in science and washing your hands before you eat are both safety precautions.
fact: Precautions are taken before a problem happens, not after it.
exercise: «Ruby wears goggles in science lessons.» What is this an example of? | A reward | *A precaution | A party | A test
exercise: «Sam packed a coat, as a precaution, in case it turned cold.» What does as a precaution mean here? | *Something done in advance to stop a problem | Something done after the problem | A very cold day | A kind of coat
exercise: Which of these is a safety precaution? | Eating sweets before a race | Losing your way home | Forgetting your helmet on a bike | *Washing your hands before you eat
test: «Mum put on sun cream before we went to the beach, as a precaution.» Why did Mum do this? | To get a tan faster | *To protect our skin before any harm happens | Because the beach was closed | To make the beach cooler
test: The school checks its fire ___ every term to keep everyone safe. Which word fits? | puzzle | pillow | *precautions | picture
exam: «Before the storm, the farmer moved the animals inside as a precaution.» What does precaution mean here? | Something done after the storm | A type of farm animal | *Something done in advance to protect from harm | A kind of storm
